    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are a few archetypes for your noir setting:\n\n**Salvador \"Sal\" Rossi:** A twitchy, small-time bookie who looks perpetually nervous, always wearing a cheap, ill-fitting fedora. He deals in favors and bad luck, operating out of a dimly lit bodega office. **Mickey \"The Shiv\" Jones:** A mountain of a man with permanently suspicious eyes, whose main skill is muscle and intimidation. He moves slow, but when he moves, it's with dangerous, economical violence. **Finnigan O'Malley:** A philosophical drifter who spends his nights in dive bars, usually nursing a lukewarm whiskey and talking about lost ideals. He might be low-level muscle, but he's smarter than his street cred suggests. **Teddy \"The Spark\" Vance:** The neighborhood hustler; always clean clothes, even when broke, and a slick, silver tongue. He's a petty thief who runs small confidence scams, always charming until the heat gets turned up.",
